# Layering (non-negotiable)

Clear separation of layers. Do not invent new ones.

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|-------|------|----------|
| Handler / controller | Transport, binding, validation, auth context extraction, response/error envelopes | Service/domain logic, GORM types, SQL |
| DTO | Request/response contracts and mapping at the boundary | Leak into services as persistent models |
| Service | Business logic, orchestration, transaction boundaries, authorization decisions, idempotency ownership, outbox publication | gin types, raw SQL, HTTP concerns |
| Repository | Persistence, GORM/SQL, locking, tenant/brand scoping | Business decisions, HTTP |

## Rules

- Do not leak repository or database details into handlers.
- Do not place transport-specific logic in services unless already established by project conventions.
- No GORM type in a handler signature. No gin type below the handler.
- Prefer composition over inheritance-style abstractions. Avoid unnecessary interfaces.
- Pair with machine enforcement when present: `depguard` (or equivalent) import boundaries so handlers cannot import repository packages directly.
